From 7f4798292c618c8a455fed60bb713e51a0f3305f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Robert DeLanghe <1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 20:24:23 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] feat(cursor): `path resume --harness cursor-agent` writes the
 Cursor CLI's chat store and resumes it

toolpath-cursor: agent_store writes and reads the cursor-agent store,
<config>/chats/<md5(cwd)>/<agentId>/store.db (<config>: CURSOR_CONFIG_DIR,
else XDG_CONFIG_HOME/cursor, else ~/.cursor): sha256-keyed blobs, meta['0']
as hex JSON, and a ConversationStateStructure root whose field 1 lists the
AI SDK ModelMessage blobs (model_messages, now shared with the IDE's
conversationState through the new proto module; the IDE bytes are
unchanged) and whose field 8 lists the rendered turns.
AgentStore::to_view reads one back.

path-cli: Harness::CursorAgent, a resume target only (share refuses it);
the projection keeps an existing chat with the same id. ScopedHome also
pins XDG_CONFIG_HOME and clears CURSOR_CONFIG_DIR, which the dev box sets.

toolpath-goldens: cursor-agent is a projection target (Agent::TARGETS;
ALL stays the seven recorded harnesses), with projection, round-trip and
writer snapshots and a declared writer contract (33 drops, two defects);
only cursor-agent keys were added to the existing shed/validate
snapshots. Qualifier records that moved (three in pipeline.rs, 17 in
README.md) are re-anchored with --supersedes.

CHANGELOG: the store path is under CURSOR_CONFIG_DIR / XDG, not always
~/.cursor/chats. `cursor-agent ls` lists a written chat (temp HOME, no
login); the live resume check is in pr/58-cursor-agent-resume.md, not run.
